# A window box is in the cell's own space. 0,0,0 is the cell's minimum corner. y is up. dir is the face the pane looks out of.
# The wall is three cubes: y 1-2 and 2-3 are the door, y 3-4 is the window. Same band as the door transom (3.05-3.90). y 2 is one voxel too low.
# FACE | dir | x0 | y0 | z0 | x1 | y1 | z1
FACE | north | 0.08 | 3.05 | -0.10 | 0.92 | 3.90 | 0.00
FACE | east | 1.00 | 3.05 | 0.08 | 1.10 | 3.90 | 0.92
FACE | south | 0.08 | 3.05 | 1.00 | 0.92 | 3.90 | 1.10
FACE | west | -0.10 | 3.05 | 0.08 | 0.00 | 3.90 | 0.92
# WIN | ox | oy | dir    ox,oy are cells from the room origin, which is 0,0 of the room.
WIN | 0 | 0 | north
WIN | 1 | 0 | north
